<p>These units feature a fully enclosed, climate-controlled cabin that shields paintwork from dust, debris, and extreme temperature fluctuations. The hydraulic ramp system allows for gentle, low-angle loading, significantly reducing the risk of undercarriage damage or curb strikes during the initial boarding phase.</p>
<h3>Mechanical Security and Load Stabilization</h3>
<p>Once the vehicle is positioned on the deck, static restraints are insufficient for the dynamic forces encountered during highway transit. The primary defense against longitudinal and lateral movement is the use of individual steel wheel-lock chocks.</p>
<p>These heavy-duty, high-density steel components are strategically placed against the tires to create a physical barrier that prevents rolling. Unlike rubber or plastic alternatives, steel chocks maintain their structural integrity under high stress levels, ensuring that the vehicle remains stationary regardless of sudden braking maneuvers or sharp turns on the expressway.</p>
<p>Complementing the wheel chocks is the application of high-tensile ratchet lashing straps. These straps are anchored to certified tie-down points on the carrier deck and looped securely around the vehicle's wheels.</p>
<p>The ratchet mechanism allows for precise tension calibration, ensuring that the straps are tight enough to immobilize the vehicle without crushing sensitive body panels. This combination of steel chocks and high-tensile ratchets creates a redundant safety system that effectively prevents movement during highway transit, safeguarding the vehicle from internal shifting and impact.</p>
